Sure! Here's how you might represent the described CI/CD system in UVL (Unified Variable Language):

```uvl
// Define the deployment stages and their requirements
deployment Stages {
    Build
    UnitTest
    Staging
    IntegrationTest
    SecurityScan
    Production {
        BlueGreen {
            // Double the infrastructure resources for swapping
        }
        Canary {
            Monitoring {
                RollbackTrigger
            }
        }
    }
}

// Define the pipeline rules
pipeline Rules {
    allPipelines {
        mustRun "Build"
        mustRun "UnitTest"
    }

    StagingPipeline {
        runsAfter "UnitTest"
    }

    ProductionPipeline {
        dependsOn "Staging"
        dependsOn "IntegrationTest"
        dependsOn "SecurityScan"

        hasStrategy "BlueGreen" {
            requiresDoubleResources
        }

        hasStrategy "Canary" {
            includes "Monitoring"
            hasTrigger "RollbackTrigger"
        }
    }

    HotfixPipeline {
        bypasses "Staging"
        bypasses "IntegrationTest"
        requires "ManualQAApproval"
        dependsOn "SecurityScan"
    }
}
```

This code snippet outlines the deployment stages, their dependencies, and the strategies available for each deployment type. It ensures that all necessary steps are followed according to the given requirements.